=== width 24, Join, Drop, first line None
frobnicate

A small command line
tool that frobnicates
files, quickly and with
zero configuration. See
https://example.com/frobnicate
for the full manual, or
ask in the chat.

Installation

Install from source with
a recent Rust toolchain:

  cargo install frobnicate
  frobnicate --version

Prebuilt binaries are
available for these
platforms:

• Linux, x86_64 and
  aarch64
• macOS, Apple silicon
  and Intel
• Windows, x86_64 only
  • requires the Visual
    C++ runtime
  • no ARM build yet

Usage

  frobnicate [OPTIONS] <FILE>...

Option   -q, --quiet
Meaning  Print nothing
         except errors
Default  off
────────────────────────
Option   -j, --jobs
Meaning  Number of
         parallel jobs
Default  4
────────────────────────
Option   --dry-run
Meaning  Show what would
         change, change
         nothing
Default  off

Exit codes

1. 0 when every file was
   processed.
2. 1 when at least one
   file failed.
3. 2 for invalid
   arguments.

│ Note Frobnication is
│ not reversible. Keep a
│ backup, or use
│ --dry-run first.

Configuration

Settings live in
frobnicate.toml:

  [defaults]
  jobs = 8
  quiet = false

Contributing

Pull requests are
welcome. Please run the
tests first, and mention
the issue number in the
title. For larger
changes, open an issue
to discuss the idea.

────────────────────────

Released under the MIT
license. Copyright (c)
the frobnicate authors.
